# Evidence-first engineering

Stay inside the accepted PRD slice and non-goals. Resolve uncertainty from: current code/tests/ADRs; pinned legacy source for parity; exact dependency/service source; then official primary documentation. Record material version-sensitive evidence. Use exact supported pins—no floating tags, prereleases, implicit majors, or configuration-based support widening.

Production code is explicit, typed, bounded, cancellable where applicable, fail-closed, and consistent with existing seams. Avoid speculative refactors/dependencies, hidden global state, placeholder success, silent fallback, and dead code.

Tests prove observable success and failure paths. Run every claimed command and distinguish unit/mock, disposable integration, live staging, and production evidence. Labels such as complete, secure, or production-ready are never evidence.
